Description: Data sets and analyses of Duchateau, Janssen and Rowlands
    (1998, ISBN:92-9146-038-9) "Linear Mixed Models: An Introduction with
    Applications in Veterinary Research", with an own engine for linear
    mixed models that gives the results of SAS PROC MIXED and PROC GLM:
    restricted and full maximum likelihood and Type 3 moment estimation of
    variance components; random coefficients with variance-component or
    unstructured covariance; compound-symmetry, first-order autoregressive,
    spatial power and unstructured residual covariance; the fixed-effects
    solution in the overparameterised coding; Type 3 and Type 1 tests with
    containment, residual, between-within, Satterthwaite (1946)
    <doi:10.2307/3002019> and Kenward and Roger (1997)
    <doi:10.2307/2533558> degrees of freedom; estimates and contrasts in
    the broad and narrow inference spaces; least-squares means with
    multiple comparisons; best linear unbiased predictions; expected mean
    squares; information criteria and likelihood ratio tests. Every
    published result of the book is reproduced and checked. With 'ggplot2'
    graphics, a plain-language interpretation of every result and a
    built-in 'shiny' application.
